{
  "schema": "mitts.jersey.v2",
  "description": "Mitts fruit league - 8 teams, each with home and away kits. Stripes are procedural horizontal bands over a UV region: pos = band center (0=top of region, 1=bottom), width = band height as a fraction of the region, both 0..1. Stripes paint in array order (later over earlier). Centered cross-section bands = stack stripes sharing pos with shrinking widths, widest first (Lime, Pomegranate, Watermelon). Asymmetric slices offset a band's pos off-center (Dragonfruit seed-line). For a cross-section to show its outer color, set the region base to that color so it reads as the skin/rind edges. 'No outline' on text = outline equal to color. yoke = top band of the torso; shoulders.color = caps at the top of the arms.",
